  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Per&#xFA; - CHS</narrative>
  </title>
  <description akvo:type="4" type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">BBB Peru</narrative>
  </description>
  <description akvo:type="6" type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CHS has more than 15 years of experience fighting against SEC and developing public and political advocacy strategies to combat it both in the field of tourism and travel, and the last two years in its online modalities. CHS also has long experience working with CSEC on the streets, especially in Loreto, where Psychosocial Legal Attention Center provides longitudinal accompaniment to victims and their families. In addition, CHS Alternativo promotes Citizen Oversight Offices, which monitor issues related to human trafficking, including its sexual purpose.
CHS has worked directly empowering young people and women in the pre and post COVID-19 context, developing their personal skills to avoid the risk of CSEC (since 2008), and to get out of it. In these efforts, since 2014 it has promoted the Fly Free Movement where private companies in the tourism sector have participated and more recently it has established alliances with technology companies for the prevention of CSEC online. The work in social organizations and actors linked to educational centers in Lima, Loreto, Madre de Dios, Cusco and Puno, have allowed CHS to support the identification and referral of cases and promotes &#x201C;protective environments&#x201D; at the community level, involving children, their families, local authorities, and social actors in the fight against this crime.

Collaboration between the Latin American partners of the DTZ Alliance through ICCO and Fly Free Movement has been consolidated since 2014, CHS will continue working at the community / grassroots organization, and with youth organizations that have been empowering throughout the implementation of the DTZ project in recent years, as part of the principle of participation. Likewise, community defenders, a group of women empowered within the framework of the DTZ, will indirectly participate.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description akvo:type="5" type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Facing SEC in DTZ implies understanding its current dimensions and taking advantage of the lessons learned to achieve lasting transformations. Therefore, taking into account the scope of the extension, based on the empowerment of children and the protective environments promoted by the DTZ, a comprehensive strategy for gathering information, political advocacy and public advocacy is implemented, which allows members to of protective environments (families, communities, public and private actors</narrative>
  </description>
